.TH "zelta\-match" "8" "" "" "System Manager\(cqs Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]zelta match\f[R] \- compare a ZFS dataset tree with its replica
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]zelta match\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]source\f[R]
\f[I]target\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]zelta match\f[R] recursively displays a dataset and its children,
the \f[I]source\f[R], and compares it to its replica, the
\f[I]target\f[R].
\f[B]zelta match\f[R] displays fields describing differences and
similarities between the two dataset trees.
This is useful for assisting with replication operations and confirming
backups.
.SH OPTIONS
\f[B]Endpoint Arguments (Required)\f[R]
.TP
\f[I]source\f[R]
Dataset tree to compare.
.TP
\f[I]target\f[R]
Replica dataset tree to compare against the source.
.PP
\f[B]Logging Options\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]\-v, \-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase verbosity.
Specify once for operational detail, twice (\f[CR]\-vv\f[R]) for debug
output.
.TP
\f[B]\-q, \-\-quiet\f[R]
Decrease log level.
Specify once to suppress notices, twice (\f[CR]\-qq\f[R]) to suppress
warnings.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-log\-level\f[R] \f[I]LEVEL\f[R]
Specify a log level value 0\-4: errors (0), warnings (1), notices (2,
default), info (3, verbose), and debug (4).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-log\-mode\f[R] \f[I]MODE\f[R]
Enable the specified log mode.
Currently supported: \f[CR]text\f[R] and \f[CR]json\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-text\f[R]
Force default output notices to print as plain text standard output.
.TP
\f[B]\-n, \-\-dryrun, \-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Display \f[CR]zfs\f[R] commands without executing them.
.PP
\f[B]Dataset and Snapshot Options\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]\-d, \-\-depth\f[R] \f[I]LEVELS\f[R]
Limit recursion depth.
For example, a depth of 1 includes only the specified dataset.
.TP
\f[B]\-X, \-\-exclude\f[R] \f[I]PATTERN\f[R]
Exclude datasets or source snapshots matching the specified pattern.
This option can include multiple patterns separated by commas and can be
specified multiple times.
See \f[I]INCLUDE AND EXCLUDE PATTERNS\f[R] in
\f[B]zelta\-options(7)\f[R] for details.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-include\f[R] \f[I]PATTERN\f[R]
Include only datasets or source snapshots matching the specified
pattern.
This option can include multiple patterns separated by commas and can be
specified multiple times.
See \f[I]INCLUDE AND EXCLUDE PATTERNS\f[R] in
\f[B]zelta\-options(7)\f[R] for details.
.PP
\f[B]Columns and Summary Behavior\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]\-H\f[R]
Suppress column headers and separate columns with a single tab.
.TP
\f[B]\-p\f[R]
Output sizes in exact numbers instead of human\-readable values like
\f[CR]1M\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-o\f[R] \f[I]FIELD\f[R][,\&...]
Specify a list of \f[B]zelta match\f[R] columns.
See \f[I]FIELD OPTIONS\f[R] below for detail.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-written\f[R]
Calculate data sizes for datasets and snapshots.
Enabled by default, but it can impact list time.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-time\f[R]
Calculate the time of each \f[CR]zfs list\f[R] operation.
